Declare V1SF among the mode attribute values

The SMALLF mode iterator can expand insns with mode V1SF, which the
define_attr "mode" list never included. gcc hosts constant-fold the
insns' (false) TARGET_HARD_FLOAT conditions and prune the V1SF
variants before genattrtab validates attribute values; clang does
not fold the conditions, so genattrtab rejects the file. The insns
remain disabled by their run-time conditions either way.

--- a/gcc/config/riscv/riscv.md
+++ b/gcc/config/riscv/riscv.md
@@ -228,7 +228,7 @@
   (const_string "unknown"))
 
 ;; Main data type used by the insn
-(define_attr "mode" "unknown,none,QI,HI,SI,DI,TI,HF,OHF,SF,DF,TF,V2HI,V4QI,V2HF,V2OHF"
+(define_attr "mode" "unknown,none,QI,HI,SI,DI,TI,HF,OHF,SF,DF,TF,V1SF,V2HI,V4QI,V2HF,V2OHF"
   (const_string "unknown"))
 
 ;; True if the main data type is twice the size of a word.
